<!--
TEMPLATE: Markdown review report. The HTML twin is report.html.tmpl (same sections, same placeholder names).

Template choice: see SKILL.md, step 5.

WRITING RULES
- No praise, no hedging words (could, maybe, might, consider), no intro. Flat claims.
- Always write the FULL sha, never a short one.
- Findings are numbered continuously across all sections. Omit empty sections.
- Effect: one sentence, at most three, each at most 15 words. Effect + Fix at most 45 words.
- Code excerpt: at most 10 lines, real line numbers, taken with
  `git show <sha>:<file> | sed -n 'a,bp'`. The breaking line ends with `<-- here`.

LABELS
- CI jobs: [OK] [FAIL] [SKIPPED]
- Criteria: [OK] mechanical (command + result) · [OK-IMAGE] screenshot as proof, check command beside
  it, base + head images for UI changes · [CODE-ONLY] static analysis only, app did not run, with
  reason · [MISSING] not met, see finding · [NOT-CHECKABLE] reason
- Re-review: [RESOLVED] [OPEN]
- Verdict: fix first | approve with suggestions | approve
- Next step by verdict: fix first -> "Fix the blocking findings, then request a re-review of the
  delta <head_sha>..HEAD"; approve with suggestions -> "Merge allowed. <n> can-fix findings may
  become follow-up issues."; approve -> "Merge allowed."
- Run section: one row per role (main reviewer, each angle or verifier agent, report writer).
  Effort is "unknown" when the runtime does not report it, never guessed.
-->

